mlab-node (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Configure the node at install time through debconf: the installer asks
    for every setting in /etc/mlab/mlab-node.env and the API key, pre-filled
    with the current value or, on a fresh install, a guess derived from the
    host (public IPs, default-route interface, link speed, virtualization
    detection). The API key is echoed as typed. "dpkg-reconfigure mlab-node" asks
    again; debconf-set-selections preseeds unattended installs.
  * /etc/mlab/mlab-node.env and /etc/mlab/api-key.env are now generated by
    the postinst from the answers (they are no longer conffiles); existing
    files and their extra settings are kept and edited in place.
  * Start the stack automatically once the configuration is complete.
  * Drop the ORGANIZATION setting: the organization belongs to the API key
    on the Autojoin side. register-ready now derives it from the registered
    hostname into /run/mlab/metadata/registration.env for jostler and
    ndt-server.
  * Ask whether to enable unattended upgrades (default: yes) for the
    distribution's security updates and the mlab-node package, via
    /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52mlab-node-unattended-upgrades. Depend on
    unattended-upgrades and iproute2.

 -- Measurement Lab <support@measurementlab.net>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

mlab-node (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: native Debian packaging of the M-Lab BYOS node stack.
    The components run as hardened, sandboxed systemd services. Component
    binaries are built from the pinned upstream sources at build time.

 -- Measurement Lab <support@measurementlab.net>  Mon, 29 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
